  "name": "DPX Electronics Case",
  "slug": "dpx-electronics-case",
  "teaser": "Adds a custom electronics storage case for SPT 4.0.13, sold by Skier LL1.",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/ArL0G1VwjIZKh8hVWP57gtjO4v5OB8Zt0XbTppTI.jpg",
  "downloads": 2167,
  "favourites_count": 29,
  "description": "<h1>DPX Electronics Case</h1>\n<p>Adds a dedicated electronics storage case to SPT.</p>\n<p>The DPX Electronics Case is designed for players who want a cleaner stash without mixing CPUs, RAM sticks, SSDs, circuit boards, military electronics and tech loot into a general junk box.</p>\n<h2>Features</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>New custom container: <strong>DPX Electronics Case</strong></li>\n<li>Sold by <strong>Skier LL1</strong></li>\n<li>Price: <strong>500,000₽</strong></li>\n<li>External size: <strong>3x3</strong></li>\n<li>Internal storage: <strong>10x10</strong></li>\n<li>Custom graphite / PCB-style texture</li>\n<li>Strict electronics whitelist</li>\n<li>No BepInEx plugin required</li>\n<li>Does not modify <code>SPT_Data</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Accepted item types</h2>\n<p>The case is made for electronic and tech items, including:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>CPU</li>\n<li>CPU Fan</li>\n<li>RAM</li>\n<li>SSD</li>\n<li>HDD</li>\n<li>Powerbank</li>\n<li>Printed Circuit Board</li>\n<li>Military Circuit Board</li>\n<li>Military Cable</li>\n<li>VPX</li>\n<li>Virtex</li>\n<li>RFID Reader</li>\n<li>COFDM</li>\n<li>Microcontroller Board</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Installation</h2>\n<p>Extract the ZIP into your SPT root folder.</p>\n<p>Expected structure:</p>\n<p>SPT/\nuser/\nmods/\nDPX-ElectronicsCase/</p>\n",
  "detail_url": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/2769/dpx-electronics-case",
  "fika_compatibility": false,
  "featured": false,
  "contains_ads": false,
  "contains_ai_content": true,
  "custom_ai_disclosure": "<p>AI was used as an assistant during development to help generate code, debug SPT compatibility issues, create documentation text, and design visual assets such as the thumbnail and custom case texture. The final mod was tested manually in-game before release.</p>\n",
